 "verdict_rules": "fits only if all hold: (1) the latency scan has a distinct peak, z = (max - median) / (1.4826 MAD) >= 4; (2) at that L the Doppler curve beats a flat line on the same frames by >= 15 %; (3) the predicted Doppler swing in the scored frames is >= 2 log bins (else the shape is untestable); (4) the camera scores >= 0.9 of the heat-map peak; (5) the fit reaches >= 0.5 of what the recording's own clear stack (cfg event) scores along a flat line, i.e. there is a ridge at all. Rule 5 was added after seeing G-BONT pass rules 1-4 with no visible ridge under its curve.",
 "reading_note": "Read off spec_*.png and heat_*.png; not part of the verdict. N850BG: a falling tone ~170 -> ~120 Hz at audio ~625-685 s, with x2 (~340 -> ~235 Hz), lies under the predicted curve. Its heat map shows the band through the camera and the mirror band ~5.3 km east across the track (the peak; camera 0.95 of it). AUR507: a falling tone ~93 -> ~84 Hz at audio ~4108-4135 s, with x2 (~185 -> ~170 Hz), lies under the curve on the approach half. After ~4140 s the curve flattens onto a steady ~76 Hz line that is also present before the pass (a non-Doppler source), so the receding half is no independent match. Its latency scan is a broad plateau, the along-track / L trade-off, so rule 1 fails. Its heat map shows the two mirror blobs, the camera and one 2.4 km across the track (the peak; camera 0.99 of it). Only 2 ADS-B reports fall within 30 s of its CPA; the 48 s gaps either side are bridged (max_gap 60). The two turboprops' L ranges within 10 % of their scan maxima (0-5 s, 6.5-12.75 s) do not overlap: no consistent L. PIPE65 and RRR6139 score about a quarter of the turboprops (no ridge to fit). A diagnostic scan over L = -20..30 s (diag_L_-20_30/) keeps both maxima (0.25 s, 11.5 s), so N850BG's peak is not an edge effect, but its z drops to 1.4 there: z depends on the scan range.",
 "verdict": "fits: N850BG"
}